WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.340
The oldest widely accepted fossils of
life are about 3.48 billion years old.

2
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:10.800
They are stromatolites:
layered mats built by bacteria.

3
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.130
Much later, a cell took in a bacterium.

4
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.870
It did not digest it.

5
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.360
The bacterium lived on inside.

6
00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.240
Its descendants are in your cells now.

7
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.630
But no one was there to see it happen.

8
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.430
So how can anyone know that it happened?

9
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.190
In this mission, you'll see how
rocks and fossils are dated,

10
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.300
and why a fossil gives only a minimum age.

11
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.620
Then you'll test the story the
way scientists test any theory.

12
00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:42.490
Your mission: find out how anyone can
know that your cells hold descendants of

13
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.470
bacteria.
